I’m thinking we might need to make the hitTestKey explicit for the quote background so it covers the entire area. While the TextSelectionSurface supports hitTestKey, the _TextBlockRenderer doesn’t expose that. I wonder if we could add a GlobalKey in _QuoteBlockSurface, but there's an issue since _TextSelectionSurface is built before the quote wrapper. Should I modify _TextBlockRenderer to create a GlobalKey? It is Stateless, so it wouldn’t persist but would register each build. Existing _TextSelectionSurface has a hitTestKey property, which could be passed to the quote text surface.
